Third-party licences: the Rust crates in Celari's wallet engine
===============================================================

Celari's wallet engine (vendor/webzjs-wallet and vendor/webzjs-keys, the WebAssembly the
app loads) is built from ChainSafe WebZjs, Celari's patches and Celari's port of
zcash_client_memory (engine/ in https://github.com/Kubudak90/zcash-wallet) and from the
Rust crates listed below (procedural macros used while compiling included), each under
the licence shown with it. Where a crate offers a choice of licences, Celari uses it under
one of them. Each licence text a crate ships is reproduced below with its copyright notice;
for a crate that ships none, the licence's standard text is.

Also compiled in: the Rust standard library (MIT OR Apache-2.0, The Rust Project
Developers), the JavaScript glue generated by wasm-bindgen (MIT OR Apache-2.0), and the
C library libsecp256k1 inside secp256k1-sys. WebZjs's own notice and libsecp256k1's are
at the end of this file.

This file is generated by scripts/gen-licenses.sh (cargo-about) from
engine/webzjs.Cargo.lock; do not edit it by hand.

